(1) capture, named encoding
   phi = Ey~(y=x); lgg(phi(0), phi(S0)) = ex(y,not(eq(y,z0))) ; equals sigma_phi: True
   capture z:=y gives ex(y,not(eq(y,y))) ; instance of lgg: True ; sentence: True
   truth of Ey~(y=y) in all pure-equality structures of size 1..5: [False, False, False, False, False]
   truth of Ey~(y=c) (closed instance, c any element) in sizes 1..5: [False, True, True, True, True]
   phi = Ey(y=Sx): lgg ex(y,eq(y,S(z0))) ; capture ex(y,eq(y,S(y))) ; instance of lgg: True ; (Ax Ey(y=Sx) is true in N, Ey(y=Sy) is false in N: S has no fixed point)

(2) decomposition of inst(sigma_phi) over substituted terms of size <= 3
   phi                       total  closed   param capture | pred(sentences) pred(params) | free occurrences of x: binder sets
   Ey~(y=x)                     40       4      14      12 | capture sentences  10 (pred True ) capture formulas (pred True ) | [['y']]
   Ey(y=Sx)                     40       4      14      12 | capture sentences  10 (pred True ) capture formulas (pred True ) | [['y']]
   x=x & Ay(x=y)                40       4      14      12 | capture sentences   0 (pred False) capture formulas (pred True ) | [[], [], ['y']]
   Ay(y=x -> x=y)               40       4      14      12 | capture sentences  10 (pred True ) capture formulas (pred True ) | [['y'], ['y']]
   x+0=x  (no binder)           40       4      14       0 | capture sentences   0 (pred False) capture formulas (pred False) | [[], []]
   Ax(x=x) & x=0                40       4      14       0 | capture sentences   0 (pred False) capture formulas (pred False) | [[]]
   Ay(x+y=y+x) & Ex(x=0)        40       4      14      12 | capture sentences  10 (pred True ) capture formulas (pred True ) | [['y'], ['y']]

(3) most specific guards from the family {closed(z), nobound(z)} (named encoding, phi = Ey~(y=x))
   data terms ['0', 'S(0)']                lgg ex(y,not(eq(y,z0)))    learned guards ['closed(z)', 'nobound(z)']
       accept z := S(S(0))    (closed   ): True
       accept z := q          (parameter): False
       accept z := y          (capture  ): False
       accept z := add(y,p)   (capture  ): False
       unguarded H1 verifier would accept the capture instance Ey~(y=y): True
   data terms ['0', 'S(0)', 'add(p,S(0))'] lgg ex(y,not(eq(y,z0)))    learned guards ['nobound(z)']
       accept z := S(S(0))    (closed   ): True
       accept z := q          (parameter): True
       accept z := y          (capture  ): False
       accept z := add(y,p)   (capture  ): False
       unguarded H1 verifier would accept the capture instance Ey~(y=y): True

(4) de Bruijn first-order encoding, phi = E~(#0 = x)
   lgg ex(not(eq(#0,z0))) ; capture E~(#0=#0) instance of lgg: True
   learned guard "no loose index in z" (true on both data): True ; capture value #0 satisfies it: False
   lambda convention (values have no loose indices, free names = parameters): capture impossible by sort.
